      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Confidently establishing the diagnosis of occupational asthma (OA) is a complicated undertaking, because it requires that the patient's asthma symptoms are caused exclusively (or at least in large part) by occupational exposures. Asthma is a common disease, and the differential diagnosis of asthma is a frequently discussed subject that includes common and uncommon disorders. This article presents a broad characterization of OA, including the elements necessary to establish a diagnosis. Differential diagnosis also is discussed."},
